intuition:
Scatter plot is like birdwatching. You see a flock (cluster). One bird flies far away (outlier). Some birds fly in a V shape (linear). Others in a spiral (nonlinear). Without looking, you'd just have a list of bird positions. The plot makes the pattern obvious.

